ruanPkg: describe the stock ramoops region (0x80D00000, 2 MiB) as reserved, uncached, so DarwinBoot can read it (0003)

Apply in uefi-ruan (git apply -p1). The range 0x80C01000-0x82A00000 was not in the map at all, so nothing used it before;
reserved memory is never part of DarwinBoot's window or XNU's memory-outside ranges (both take EfiConventionalMemory only).

--- a/Platforms/Xiaomi/ruanPkg/Library/MemoryMapLib/MemoryMapLib.c
+++ b/Platforms/Xiaomi/ruanPkg/Library/MemoryMapLib/MemoryMapLib.c
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@
   {"XBL Log",           0x808E4000, 0x0001C000, AddMem, MEM_RES, UNCACHEABLE, Reserv, UNCACHED_UNBUFFERED_XN},
   {"CPUCP FW",          0x80B00000, 0x00100000, AddMem, SYS_MEM, SYS_MEM_CAP, Reserv, UNCACHED_UNBUFFERED_XN},
   {"Chip Info",         0x80C00000, 0x00001000, AddMem, MEM_RES, UNCACHEABLE, Reserv, UNCACHED_UNBUFFERED_XN},
+  // Android's pstore (stock DT ramoops@80D00000: 2 x 256 KiB dmesg, 512 KiB console at 0x80D80000, 1 MiB pmsg). Mapped so
+  // DarwinBoot's USB receiver can send it back (fastboot get_staged); reserved, so nothing in UEFI or XNU allocates it.
+  {"RAM Oops",          0x80D00000, 0x00200000, AddMem, MEM_RES, UNCACHEABLE, Reserv, UNCACHED_UNBUFFERED_XN},
   {"WLAN FW",           0x82A00000, 0x00C00000, AddMem, MEM_RES, UNCACHEABLE, Reserv, UNCACHED_UNBUFFERED_XN},
   {"PIL Reserved",      0x84B00000, 0x1C900000, AddMem, MEM_RES, UNCACHEABLE, Reserv, UNCACHED_UNBUFFERED_XN},
   {"Display Demura",    0xA1400000, 0x02B00000, AddMem, MEM_RES, SYS_MEM_CAP, Reserv, WRITE_THROUGH_XN},
